# Code Style & Quality

## Standard & flags

- **C11** (`-std=c11`)
- `-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Werror`
- `-D_POSIX_C_SOURCE=200809L`
- Zero warnings — all treated as errors

## Formatting

- **Indentation:** 4 spaces. No tabs.
- **Function definitions:** opening brace on its own line.
- **Line length:** prefer ≤80 characters where practical.
- **Files end with a single newline.**

## Module conventions

- **`src/main.c`** stays thin — wiring only; parse flags, collect operands, call
  `file_toto_run()`. No `stat`/`open`/`read`, no magic matching.
- **`include/file_toto.h`** — `static inline classify_content()` is intentional
  (shared by `file_toto_identify.c` and tests without linking full `src/`).
- **One concern per `src/file_toto_*.c`** — do not collapse back into a monolith
  without reason.
- **Platform code:** use `#if defined(_WIN32)` / `#else` for OS-specific behaviour
  (e.g. symlink/`lstat` availability, binary-mode opens on Windows).

## Naming

| Kind | Style | Examples |
|------|-------|----------|
| Functions | `snake_case` | `file_toto_run`, `classify_content`, `match_magic` |
| Macros / constants | `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` | `FILE_TOTO_BUF_SIZE`, `FILE_TOTO_DESC_CAP` |
| Headers | `FILE_TOTO_*_H` guards | `FILE_TOTO_H`, `FILE_TOTO_CLI_H` |
| Struct types | `snake_case` + `_t` suffix | `file_toto_opts_t` |

Public API prefix: **`file_toto_`** for module entry points; `classify_content`
is the spec name for the inline classification helper.

## Memory

- **Per-file path:** stack only — `unsigned char buf[FILE_TOTO_BUF_SIZE]` for the
  content prefix; stack description buffer `char desc[FILE_TOTO_DESC_CAP]`.
- No heap in the classify / identify path.
- No `realloc` in-tree. Avoid `malloc` unless an explicitly justified pre-loop
  need appears (none in the baseline design).

## I/O rules (`file_toto_identify.c`)

- `open` / `read` / `close` (and `stat` / `lstat`) for classification input.
- Result lines go to stdout via `write(STDOUT_FILENO, …)` with partial-write and
  `EINTR` retry — not `printf` / `fprintf` / `puts` / `fputs` / `fwrite`.
- `read()` and `write()` byte counts must **never** be ignored.
- Do not ignore `EINTR` on `read`/`write` — retry.

## Errors

- **stderr only** for true diagnostics: `file-toto: <context>: <strerror(errno)>`
- Cannot-open / unreadable file messages that POSIX/`file(1)` print as the
  classification result belong on **stdout** as the result line (see
  `implementation.mdc`), not as a substitute for stderr errno diagnostics.
- Implemented in `file_toto_emit.c` for stderr; result formatting in identify.

## Comments

- Chain-of-thought block at top of each `src/*.c` and test file (see existing
  files once present).
- Contract comments on non-trivial functions: preconditions, postconditions,
  return value, error behaviour.
- Comment non-obvious decisions (buffer size, magic order, platform guards);
  not obvious code.

## Tests

- Plain `assert()` — no external test framework.
- One scenario per `tests/test_classify_*.c`; runner in `tests/test_runner.c`.
- Print `PASS: <name>` on success.

## What not to do

- Do not compile as C++.
- Do not link libraries beyond libc (no libmagic, no zlib).
- Do not use `gets`, unbounded `scanf`, or ignore `read()` / `write()` byte counts.
- Do not add single-dash `-h` / `-v` as help/version aliases (meta flags are
  `--help` / `--h` and `--version` / `--v` only; `-h` / `-L` are real `file`
  options — see `project-overview.mdc`).
- Do not load external magic databases (`-m`) unless explicitly requested.
- Do not use stdio formatting in the identify/write-result path — project
  standard is raw `write()`.
